   "evidence": "Channel.lean:294-299 \u2014 the proof body is `have := c.L_eq_J_or_S_eq_one; rw [parity_eq_one_iff, Nat.even_iff] at hP; rw [Nat.odd_iff] at hJ; omega`, which only ever compares `L % 2` with `J % 2`; `L_eq_J_or_S_eq_one` (line 164) supplies the rest.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Nuclei/Light/Channel.lean",
   "fix": "State it as `(h : \u00ac(Even c.L \u2194 Even c.J)) : c.S = 1 \u2227 (c.L + 1 = c.J \u2228 c.L = c.J + 1)` (equivalently `c.parity \u2260 (-1) ^ c.J`) and derive the current odd-`J`/positive-parity form from it via `parity_eq_one_iff`; the downstream users `eq_tripletS1_or_eq_tripletD1_iff` (line 305) and `pauliAllowed_iff_isospin_eq_zero_of_odd_J_of_parity_eq_one` (line 316) keep their present signatures.",
   "issue": "`S_eq_one_and_L_add_one_eq_J_or_L_eq_J_add_one_of_odd_J_of_parity_eq_one` assumes `Odd c.J` and `c.parity = 1`, but the proof uses only that `L` and `J` have opposite parity (`L_eq_J_or_S_eq_one` plus `hP : L % 2 = 0`, `hJ : J % 2 = 1`, then `omega`). The restriction drops the other half of the same statement \u2014 even `J` with odd `L`, i.e. the standard \u00b3P\u2082/\u00b3F\u2082, \u00b3F\u2084/\u00b3H\u2084 unnatural-parity channels \u2014 which the module's own general-`J` `IsTensorPair` API otherwise covers.",
   "line": 294
  }
